From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0307: kern.sweet_boot_android restarts into the system, not fastboot

0221 makes every restart go to the bootloader by default (iOS was only ever started with fastboot boot,
and a plain restart would have come up in Android). The switch to Android (0305/0306) restarted that
way too: the slot and the boot LUN were right, the phone stopped in fastboot, `fastboot continue` booted
Android. The switch now sets the restart mode to the system first. Dual-boot images (iOS in its own
slot) are packed with boot-arg sweet_reboot=0, so iOS's own restarts come back to iOS.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
index 1d1825a..b4ded34 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
@@ -1302,6 +1302,7 @@ out_free:
 }
 
 extern int reboot_kernel(int howto, char *message);
+extern void sweet_reboot_mode_set(int mode);
 
 static int
 sysctl_sweet_boot_android SYSCTL_HANDLER_ARGS
@@ -1322,6 +1323,8 @@ sysctl_sweet_boot_android SYSCTL_HANDLER_ARGS
 	}
 	error = sweet_ufs_slot(active == 'a' ? 'b' : 'a', false, NULL);
 	if (!error && v == 1) {
+		/* 0307: a restart to the system (the slot just made active), not the default bootloader (0221) */
+		sweet_reboot_mode_set(0);
 		(void)reboot_kernel(0, (char *)"sweet: to Android");
 	}
 	return error;
